<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">25 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 25 November, from 1034 to 1975.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1034</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Malcolm II of Scotland dies</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Malcolm II died after a 29-year reign and was succeeded by his grandson Duncan I. Duncan was killed in battle by Macbeth in 1040, events Shakespeare reworked freely more than five centuries later.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1783</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The last British troops leave New York City</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">British forces evacuated New York, their last stronghold in the United States, and George Washington led the Continental Army into the city. 'Evacuation Day' was celebrated in New York for over a century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-york">New York</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1863</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Union troops storm Missionary Ridge</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Chattanooga, Union soldiers charged up Missionary Ridge beyond their orders and routed Braxton Bragg's Confederate army. The victory opened the way into Georgia.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1947</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Hollywood studios blacklist the 'Hollywood Ten'</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Studio heads issued the Waldorf Statement, refusing to employ ten writers and directors cited for contempt of Congress. The Hollywood blacklist that followed ended or interrupted hundreds of careers.</p></li><li class="tih-event-card"><p class="tih-event-year">1975</p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Suriname gains independence from the Netherlands</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The former colony of Dutch Guiana on South America's north coast became the independent Republic of Suriname. Around a third of its population emigrated to the Netherlands.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/suriname">Suriname</a></div></li></ol>
